    "title": "Former Grady County Schools Superintendent dies at 74 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By WCTV Staff ,\n8 hours ago GRADY COUNTY, Ga. (WCTV) - A former Grady County Superintendent died Monday, according to the school district. Dr. Thomas James ‘Tommy’ Pharis is reportedly from Thomasville and was born in Cairo in 1951. He was Grady County’s Superintendent from 2007 to 2013, per previous reporting from our sister station WALB. Read full article",
